A kind gesture. Nothing more.

I told myself this and almost believed it. Aldren was courteous — bred for it, trained in it, a sun-knight who radiated warmth the way a hearth radiates heat: constantly, generously, without discrimination. The kiss on the knuckles was a performance of gallantry, not a declaration of passion, and the speech about standing beside me was the sort of thing any well-schooled suitor would say.

I tucked the rose into the breast of the tunic-dress and straightened my spine. Time to move on.

